---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { business, primaryInstructor } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Lesson terms | Route 66 Driving School" description="Booking, payment and cancellation terms for Route 66 Driving School lessons.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Lesson terms</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 3 October 2026. These terms apply to all lessons and test-day bookings with {business.name}.</p>

      <h2>Before your first lesson</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You need to be 17 or over (16 if you get the higher rate mobility component of PIP) and hold a valid provisional or full driving licence.</li>
        <li>Please show us your licence at your first lesson.</li>
        <li>You must meet the eyesight standard: read a number plate from 20 metres, with glasses or lenses if you need them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Lessons and payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lessons are two hours long unless we agree otherwise.</li>
        <li>Lessons are paid for in advance. Block bookings are paid when booked.</li>
        <li>The price we quote is the full price, including any early-morning test surcharge.</li>
        <li>Lesson time starts and ends at the agreed pick-up point.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your right to cancel within 14 days</h2>
      <p>
        If you book by phone or WhatsApp, you can cancel within 14 days of booking for a full refund. If you ask us
        to start lessons within those 14 days and then cancel, we'll refund what you paid minus the lessons you've already
        had.
      </p>

      <h2>Moving or cancelling a lesson</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give us at least 48 hours' notice and we'll move your lesson or refund it in full.</li>
        <li>
          If you cancel with less than 48 hours' notice or miss a lesson, we may charge up to the full lesson fee to cover
          our loss. We won't charge if we fill the slot, and we're understanding about illness and emergencies.
        </li>
        <li>
          If we have to cancel, we'll give you as much notice as we can and offer another time or a full refund. If we
          cancel with less than 48 hours' notice, your next lesson of the same length is free.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Block bookings and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for unused hours to be refunded at any time. We refund within 14 days, charging the hours you've
        used at our standard hourly rate shown on your quote, so you only lose the block discount on hours actually
        taken.
      </p>

      <h2>Driving tests in our car</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You book and pay DVSA for your test. Please check the date and time with us before booking so we can confirm the car is free.</li>
        <li>
          We may refuse to take you to your test if we think you're not yet ready to drive safely on your own, or if the
          car can't be used for reasons outside our control. If we do, we'll explain why and refund our test-day charge in
          full.
        </li>
        <li>
          If your test is lost through our fault, for example an instructor absence or a breakdown we could have avoided,
          we'll also reimburse your DVSA test fee.
        </li>
        <li>
          If DVSA cancels your test, any refund of the test fee comes from DVSA. Our test-day charge carries over to your
          new date, or we'll refund it if you prefer.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Safety and conduct</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We won't give a lesson if we think you're under the influence of alcohol or drugs, and you'll still be charged for it.</li>
        <li>Lessons are given in dual-control cars insured for driving tuition.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If something isn't right, please tell us first and we'll try to sort it out by phone or WhatsApp on
        {primaryInstructor.phoneDisplay}. If you're still not happy, you can contact Citizens Advice, or report concerns about an instructor's conduct to
        DVSA at <a href="mailto:instructorconduct@dvsa.gov.uk">instructorconduct@dvsa.gov.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <p>Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
